{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Predicting NBA Fouls: Scouting the Referees\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"Technical Report — Multiple Linear Regression\"\n",
        "author: \"Jackson Ferry, Jake Hough, Whitney Holt\"\n",
        "date: today\n",
        "format:\n",
        "    typst:\n",
        "        fontsize: 9pt\n",
        "        toc: true\n",
        "        section-numbering: \"1.1\"\n",
        "        margin:\n",
        "            x: 1.5cm\n",
        "            y: 2cm\n",
        "execute:\n",
        "    warning: false   ## keep package warnings out of the PDF\n",
        "    message: false\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "# Plan\n",
        "\n",
        "## Business Objective\n",
        "\n",
        "NBA teams spend significant time scouting opponents, but rarely scout the officials. Referee crews differ in how tightly they call games: some crews call many fouls, while others \"let the players play.\" The number of fouls in a game affects free-throw points, foul trouble for key players, and how physical a team can afford to be on defense.\n",
        "\n",
        "The decision we want to inform is a **pre-game coaching decision**. The referee crew for every NBA game is published at 9:00 AM ET on game day. Using that crew, a coaching staff must decide how many fouls to plan for and adjust its game plan accordingly (rotations for foul-prone players and how physical to play on defense).\n",
        "\n",
        "Our objective is therefore to **predict the total number of personal fouls called in a regular-season game before tip-off**, and to quantify how much of that total is driven by the referee crew compared with the two teams.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Actions and States of the World\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Actions ($a$):** the number of fouls the coaching staff plans for, and the matching game plan. In practice this is grouped into three plans: *physical defense* (low-foul crew expected), *standard plan*, and *protect foul-prone players / safer defense* (high-foul crew expected).\n",
        "* **States of the world ($\\theta$):** the true number of fouls that will be called in the game, which is unknown before tip-off.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Loss Function\n",
        "\n",
        "We formalize the objective with **quadratic (squared error) loss**:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\ell(a, \\theta) = (a - \\theta)^2\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "where $a$ is the planned (predicted) number of total fouls and $\\theta$ is the actual number of total fouls. We chose quadratic loss over linear utility for two reasons:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Large misses hurt more than small misses.** Under-planning by 2 fouls is a minor inconvenience; under-planning by 10 fouls can put a starter on the bench with foul trouble in the third quarter. The cost of a miss grows faster than linearly.\n",
        "2. **Misses in both directions are costly.** Planning for too many fouls makes a team play too passively; planning for too few leads to foul trouble. Quadratic loss is symmetric.\n",
        "\n",
        "Under quadratic loss, the action that minimizes expected loss is the **mean** of the predictive distribution, $a^* = E[\\theta \\mid X]$. This aligns directly with ordinary least squares, which estimates the conditional mean by minimizing squared error. The mean squared error (MSE) on held-out games is therefore our decision-theoretic measure of fit.\n",
        "\n",
        "To translate fouls into a business quantity, we also convert fouls into **free-throw points**. *Assumption:* each foul produces about 1.1 free-throw attempts on average, and NBA teams make about 78% of free throws, so\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\text{free-throw points} \\approx 0.85 \\times \\text{fouls}.\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "This conversion is approximate and is used only to communicate the size of the crew effect, not to estimate the model.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Ideal Data and the Data Story\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data story.** Before a game, the league assigns a crew of three referees. Each referee has a personal tendency to call more or fewer fouls. The two teams also have their own tendencies to commit fouls (style of play, roster, pace). The game context matters too: overtime adds playing time, and the end of the season may change effort and rotations. League-wide rule emphasis changes from season to season. Total fouls in the game are the result of all of these factors plus random game-to-game variation.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Ideal data.** One row per game with:\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Outcome ($Y$):** total personal fouls called in the game (both teams combined).\n",
        "* **Predictors ($X$):** each referee's foul tendency measured *before* the game, the crew's experience and any home/road bias, each team's foul tendency measured before the game, overtime periods, timing in the season, and the season.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Build\n",
        "\n",
        "## Model Specification\n",
        "\n",
        "Because we expect the factors above to add together, and because total fouls are continuous and roughly bell-shaped (shown in the Explore section), we start with a multiple linear regression:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\\begin{aligned}\n",
        "\\text{total\\_fouls}_i = \\;& \\beta_0 + \\beta_1\\,\\text{crew\\_fouls}_i + \\beta_2\\,\\text{crew\\_experience}_i + \\beta_3\\,\\text{crew\\_foul\\_diff}_i + \\beta_4\\,\\text{crew\\_home\\_win\\_pct}_i \\\\\n",
        "& + \\beta_5\\,\\text{home\\_team\\_fouls}_i + \\beta_6\\,\\text{away\\_team\\_fouls}_i + \\beta_7\\,\\text{overtime}_i + \\beta_8\\,\\text{late\\_season}_i \\\\\n",
        "& + \\sum_{s} \\gamma_s\\,\\text{season}_{s,i} + \\epsilon_i, \\qquad \\epsilon_i \\sim \\text{Normal}(0, \\sigma^2)\n",
        "\\end{aligned}\n",
        "$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Simplifying assumptions:**\n",
        "\n",
        "* **Crew averaging.** The three referees' tendencies are averaged into one crew value. This assumes each referee contributes equally to the crew's total, regardless of role (crew chief vs. crew member).\n",
        "* **Linear, additive effects.** Each factor adds a fixed number of fouls, regardless of the other factors (no interactions).\n",
        "* **Normal errors.** Fouls are counts, so a Poisson model would be the natural choice for count data. Because total fouls are large counts (around 40) and approximately bell-shaped, the normal approximation is reasonable, and we stay within ordinary linear regression.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Simulating Ideal Data and Recovering Parameters\n",
        "\n",
        "Before using real data, we simulate data from the model above with known (\"true\") parameter values, then check that OLS recovers them. The parameter values are chosen to look like plausible NBA games; they are not estimates."
      ],
      "id": "3461b4a2"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import polars as pl\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import statsmodels.api as sm\n",
        "from pyprojroot.here import here\n",
        "from IPython.display import display\n",
        "from plotnine import *\n",
        "\n",
        "## Presentation colors - used on every chart\n",
        "nbaGreen = '#3AA845'\n",
        "nbaTheme = (theme_minimal()\n",
        "  + theme(text = element_text(size = 11),\n",
        "          plot_title = element_text(size = 13, weight = 'bold'),\n",
        "          figure_size = (8, 4.5))\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "## To fix format of PDF output\n",
        "pl.Config.set_tbl_cols(8);\n",
        "pl.Config.set_tbl_rows(10);"
      ],
      "id": "66cf2e16",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Simulate ideal data - one row per game\n",
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n",
        "nGames = 1000\n",
        "\n",
        "## True parameter values (chosen, not estimated)\n",
        "trueParams = {\n",
        "    'const': -60.0,\n",
        "    'crew_fouls_per_game': 1.5,   ## crew tendency matters most\n",
        "    'home_team_fouls': 1.0,\n",
        "    'away_team_fouls': 1.0,\n",
        "    'overtime': 5.0,              ## extra 5 minutes of play\n",
        "    'late_season': -1.5,          ## lighter effort / rotations late\n",
        "}\n",
        "sigma = 6.0                       ## game-to-game randomness\n",
        "\n",
        "simData = pl.DataFrame({\n",
        "    'crew_fouls_per_game': rng.normal(39.5, 1.7, nGames),\n",
        "    'home_team_fouls': rng.normal(19.7, 1.4, nGames),\n",
        "    'away_team_fouls': rng.normal(19.7, 1.4, nGames),\n",
        "    'overtime': rng.binomial(1, 0.06, nGames),\n",
        "    'late_season': rng.binomial(1, 0.10, nGames),\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "## Build the outcome from the model\n",
        "mu = trueParams['const'] + sum(trueParams[c] * simData[c].to_numpy() for c in simData.columns)\n",
        "simData = simData.with_columns(total_fouls = pl.Series(mu + rng.normal(0, sigma, nGames)).round(0))\n",
        "\n",
        "## Recover parameters with OLS\n",
        "X_sim = sm.add_constant(simData.drop('total_fouls').to_pandas())\n",
        "fit_sim = sm.OLS(simData['total_fouls'].to_pandas(), X_sim).fit()\n",
        "\n",
        "ciSim = fit_sim.conf_int()\n",
        "pl.DataFrame({\n",
        "    'parameter': list(trueParams.keys()),\n",
        "    'true': list(trueParams.values()),\n",
        "    'estimate': fit_sim.params[list(trueParams.keys())].round(2).tolist(),\n",
        "    'ci_low': ciSim.loc[list(trueParams.keys()), 0].round(2).tolist(),\n",
        "    'ci_high': ciSim.loc[list(trueParams.keys()), 1].round(2).tolist(),\n",
        "})"
      ],
      "id": "eea1539a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Every slope estimate is close to its true value, and every 95% confidence interval for a slope contains the true value. The intercept is less precise because it represents a game where every predictor equals zero, far outside the data, but it is not of business interest. This confirms that, if real games follow our data story, OLS can recover the effects we care about, and our code works before we use real data.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Explore\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data Sources\n",
        "\n",
        "We combined three sources into one table with one row per game:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Source | Level | What it provides | Link |\n",
        "|:--|:--|:--|:--|\n",
        "| NBAstuffer referee stats (2017–18 to 2025–26) | One row per referee per season | Fouls called per game, experience, foul differential, home-team win % | <https://www.nbastuffer.com/> |\n",
        "| NBA game referee assignments | One row per game | Teams, date, season, and the three officials | **[ADD LINK]** |\n",
        "| NBA team game logs (`nba_api`, `LeagueGameLog`) | One row per team per game | Personal fouls (`PF`) and minutes played | <https://github.com/swar/nba_api> |\n",
        "\n",
        "## Comparing Real Data to Ideal Data\n",
        "\n",
        "Our real data matches the ideal data closely on the outcome: total fouls are measured exactly for every game. The predictors differ from the ideal in three ways:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Referee tendency is a season average, not a pre-game measure.** NBAstuffer reports each referee's average for the full season, which includes the game being predicted. Ideally we would use only games before tip-off. This is a form of data leakage and likely makes the crew effect look somewhat stronger in-sample than it would be in true pre-game use. We show in the EDA that referees are consistent year to year, which supports using last season's averages for real pre-game predictions (as we do in the Lakers–Warriors example).\n",
        "2. **Team foul tendency is also a season average** computed from the game logs, with the same limitation.\n",
        "3. **Some ideal predictors are not available:** player-level fouls and minutes, foul types, and team strategy. Team foul averages act as a **proxy** for team style.\n",
        "\n",
        "Also, `overtime` is not known before tip-off. It is included as a control so the other coefficients are not distorted by longer games; for pre-game predictions we set it to zero.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Data Cleaning and Merging\n",
        "\n",
        "### Combining the Referee Stats Files Into One Table"
      ],
      "id": "3c5c2cb9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "seasons = ['2017-2018', '2018-2019', '2019-2020', '2020-2021', '2021-2022', '2022-2023', '2023-2024', '2024-2025', '2025-2026']\n",
        "\n",
        "refList = []\n",
        "for s in seasons:\n",
        "    fileName = f'nba_referee_stats_{s}.csv'\n",
        "    if s == '2025-2026':\n",
        "        fileName = 'nba_referee_stats_2025_2026.csv' ## uses an underscore instead of dash between years\n",
        "\n",
        "    refSeason = pl.read_csv(here(f'NBAFoulPredictor/Data/{fileName}'))\n",
        "\n",
        "    ## find foul differential column (the name changes across seasons)\n",
        "    diffCol = [c for c in refSeason.columns if 'FOUL DIFFERENTIAL' in c][0]\n",
        "\n",
        "    refSeason = (refSeason\n",
        "        .rename({diffCol: 'foul_diff'})\n",
        "        .rename({'TYPE': 'ROLE'}, strict = False)           ## older files say TYPE\n",
        "        .drop(['RANK', 'Unnamed: 13'], strict = False)      ## empty columns\n",
        "        .with_columns(Season = pl.lit(s))                   ## adds Season if missing\n",
        "        )\n",
        "    refList.append(refSeason)\n",
        "\n",
        "## Stack all seasons\n",
        "refStats = pl.concat(refList, how = 'diagonal')\n",
        "\n",
        "## Renaming columns\n",
        "refStats = refStats.rename({\n",
        "    'Season': 'season', 'REFEREE': 'referee', 'ROLE': 'role', 'GENDER': 'gender', 'EXPERIENCE (YEARS)': 'experience', 'GAMES OFFICIATED': 'games', 'HOME TEAM WIN%': 'home_win_pct', 'HOME TEAM POINTS DIFFERENTIAL': 'home_pt_diff', 'TOTAL POINTS PER GAME': 'points_per_game', 'CALLED FOULS PER GAME': 'fouls_per_game', 'FOUL% AGAINST ROAD TEAMS': 'foul_pct_road', 'FOUL% AGAINST HOME TEAMS': 'foul_pct_home',\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "## Some seasons store percents as 53.8 instead of 0.538\n",
        "refStats = refStats.with_columns(\n",
        "    pl.when(pl.col(c) > 1).then(pl.col(c) / 100).otherwise(pl.col(c)).alias(c)\n",
        "    for c in ['foul_pct_road', 'foul_pct_home']\n",
        ")\n",
        "refStats.shape"
      ],
      "id": "09099d7a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Combining CHIEF and CREW Rows\n",
        "\n",
        "Starting in 2020–21, a referee can appear twice in a season (once as crew chief, once as crew member). We combine these rows into one row per referee per season, using a games-weighted average."
      ],
      "id": "eff2bef4"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "avgCols = ['home_win_pct', 'home_pt_diff', 'points_per_game', 'fouls_per_game', 'foul_pct_road', 'foul_pct_home', 'foul_diff']\n",
        "\n",
        "refStats = (refStats\n",
        "    .group_by(['season', 'referee'])\n",
        "    .agg(\n",
        "        experience = pl.col('experience').max(),\n",
        "        gender = pl.col('gender').first(),\n",
        "        games = pl.col('games').sum(),\n",
        "        ## games-weighted average for every column in avgCols\n",
        "        *[((pl.col(c) * pl.col('games')).sum() / pl.col('games').sum()).alias(c) for c in avgCols]\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .sort(['season', 'referee'])\n",
        ")\n",
        "refStats.shape"
      ],
      "id": "3dfe333c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Cleaning the Games File"
      ],
      "id": "8f54d788"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "games = pl.read_csv(here('NBAFoulPredictor/Data/nba_games_ref_assignments.csv'))\n",
        "\n",
        "games = (games\n",
        "    ## Split season code (22025 --> game type 2, start year 2025)\n",
        "    .with_columns(\n",
        "        game_type = pl.col('season') // 10000,\n",
        "        start_year = pl.col('season') % 10000,\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    ## Match the referee table format ('2025-2026')\n",
        "    .with_columns(\n",
        "        season = pl.col('start_year').cast(pl.String) + '-' + (pl.col('start_year') + 1).cast(pl.String)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    ## Keep only regular season games from 2017-18 on\n",
        "    .filter(pl.col('game_type') == 2, pl.col('start_year') >= 2017)\n",
        "    ## Fix team names\n",
        "    .with_columns(\n",
        "        pl.col(['home_team', 'away_team']).str.replace('L.A.', 'LA', literal = True)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    ## Remove games listed twice\n",
        "    .unique(subset = 'game_id', keep = 'first', maintain_order = True)\n",
        "    ## Remove games missing referees\n",
        "    .drop_nulls(subset = ['official1', 'official2', 'official3'])\n",
        "    ## Drop 4th referee column (empty during regular season)\n",
        "    .drop(['official4', 'official4_code', 'official4_JNum'])\n",
        ")\n",
        "games.shape"
      ],
      "id": "138b7a14",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Matching Referee Names and Building Crew Statistics\n",
        "\n",
        "Referee names are spelled differently across files, so we standardize them before joining. After the fix, every referee in every game matches a season record."
      ],
      "id": "f8ca6afc"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "nameFix = {\n",
        "    'J.T. Orr': 'JT Orr',\n",
        "    'Sharae Mitchell': \"Sha'Rae Mitchell\", 'ShaRae Mitchell': \"Sha'Rae Mitchell\",\n",
        "    'Pat OConnell': \"Pat O'Connell\", 'PAT OConnell': \"Pat O'Connell\", \"PAT O'Connell\": \"Pat O'Connell\",\n",
        "    'Cheryl Flores': 'Che Flores',\n",
        "    'Jamahl Ralls': 'JD Ralls',\n",
        "    'CP Painter': 'Chelisa Painter',\n",
        "}\n",
        "refStats = refStats.with_columns(pl.col('referee').replace(nameFix))\n",
        "\n",
        "## One row per referee per game, with that referee's season stats\n",
        "gameRefs = (games\n",
        "    .unpivot(index = ['game_id', 'season'], on = ['official1', 'official2', 'official3'],\n",
        "        variable_name = 'slot', value_name = 'referee')\n",
        "    .with_columns(pl.col('referee').replace(nameFix))\n",
        "    .join(refStats, on = ['season', 'referee'], how = 'left')\n",
        ")\n",
        "## Check - should be 0 unmatched referees\n",
        "gameRefs['fouls_per_game'].null_count()"
      ],
      "id": "d4e8f9b8",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Average the 3 referees into one crew value per game\n",
        "crewStats = (gameRefs\n",
        "    .group_by('game_id')\n",
        "    .agg(\n",
        "        crew_fouls_per_game = pl.col('fouls_per_game').mean(),\n",
        "        crew_experience = pl.col('experience').mean(),\n",
        "        crew_foul_diff = pl.col('foul_diff').mean(),\n",
        "        crew_home_win_pct = pl.col('home_win_pct').mean(),\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "games = games.join(crewStats, on = 'game_id', how = 'left')\n",
        "games.shape"
      ],
      "id": "5d16c67a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Pulling Team Game Logs\n",
        "\n",
        "The NBA API pull below was run once and saved to `Data/nba_team_game_logs.csv`, so it is commented out to avoid calling the API on every render."
      ],
      "id": "0742d8af"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# import time\n",
        "# from nba_api.stats.endpoints import leaguegamelog\n",
        "#\n",
        "# foulList = []\n",
        "# for year in range(2017, 2026):\n",
        "#     seasonCode = f'{year}-{str(year + 1)[-2:]}' ## nba_api wants '2017-18' not '2017-2018'\n",
        "#     log = leaguegamelog.LeagueGameLog(\n",
        "#         season = seasonCode,\n",
        "#         season_type_all_star = 'Regular Season',\n",
        "#         timeout = 60,\n",
        "#     )\n",
        "#     result = log.get_dict()['resultSets'][0]\n",
        "#     seasonLog = pl.DataFrame(result['rowSet'], schema = result['headers'], orient = 'row', infer_schema_length = None)\n",
        "#     foulList.append(seasonLog.select('GAME_ID', 'TEAM_ABBREVIATION', 'PF', 'MIN'))\n",
        "#     time.sleep(1) ## pause so the NBA site doesn't block us\n",
        "#\n",
        "# gameLogs = pl.concat(foulList)\n",
        "# gameLogs.write_csv(here('Data/nba_team_game_logs.csv'))\n",
        "\n",
        "gameLogs = pl.read_csv(here('NBAFoulPredictor/Data/nba_team_game_logs.csv'))\n",
        "gameLogs['MIN'].value_counts().sort('MIN')  ## 240 = regulation, each +25 = one overtime"
      ],
      "id": "f581b176",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Total Fouls Per Game (Outcome)"
      ],
      "id": "77dab745"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "totalFouls = (gameLogs\n",
        "    .with_columns(game_id = pl.col('GAME_ID').cast(pl.Int64)) ## 0021700001 --> 21700001\n",
        "    .group_by('game_id')\n",
        "    .agg(\n",
        "        total_fouls = pl.col('PF').sum(),     ## both teams' fouls added together\n",
        "        n_teams = pl.len(),                   ## should be 2 every game\n",
        "        game_minutes = pl.col('MIN').max(),\n",
        "    )\n",
        ")\n",
        "games = games.join(totalFouls, on = 'game_id', how = 'left')\n",
        "\n",
        "## Checks: every game has exactly 2 teams, and how many games have no foul total\n",
        "print(totalFouls['n_teams'].value_counts())\n",
        "print('Games missing total_fouls:', games['total_fouls'].null_count())\n",
        "games.filter(pl.col('total_fouls').is_null()).group_by('season').len()"
      ],
      "id": "d27933cc",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "All 45 games without a foul total are from the 2019–20 season, which was interrupted by COVID-19. They are 0.4% of the data, so we drop them."
      ],
      "id": "eea67c44"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "games = (games\n",
        "    .drop_nulls(subset = 'total_fouls')\n",
        "    .drop('n_teams')\n",
        ")\n",
        "games.shape"
      ],
      "id": "06850452",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Team Foul Averages (Home and Away)\n",
        "\n",
        "We first tried the NBAstuffer team fouls file, but it stops at 2024–25, which left every 2025–26 game blank. Instead, we calculated each team's season foul average ourselves from the game logs, which cover every season."
      ],
      "id": "61afcbe0"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "teamSeasonFouls = (gameLogs\n",
        "    ## Get season from game ID\n",
        "    .with_columns(start_year = 2000 + (pl.col('GAME_ID') // 100000) % 100)\n",
        "    .with_columns(\n",
        "        season = pl.col('start_year').cast(pl.String) + '-' + (pl.col('start_year') + 1).cast(pl.String)\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    ## Average fouls per game for each team in each season\n",
        "    .group_by(['season', 'TEAM_ABBREVIATION'])\n",
        "    .agg(team_fouls = pl.col('PF').mean())\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "games = (games\n",
        "    .join(teamSeasonFouls.rename({'TEAM_ABBREVIATION': 'home_team_abbr', 'team_fouls': 'home_team_fouls'}), on = ['season', 'home_team_abbr'], how = 'left')\n",
        "    .join(teamSeasonFouls.rename({'TEAM_ABBREVIATION': 'away_team_abbr', 'team_fouls': 'away_team_fouls'}), on = ['season', 'away_team_abbr'], how = 'left')\n",
        ")\n",
        "games.select(pl.col('home_team_fouls', 'away_team_fouls').null_count())"
      ],
      "id": "3a0ac346",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Final Modeling Table\n",
        "\n",
        "We create `overtime` (number of overtime periods) and `late_season` (game in the last 14 days of the regular season), keep only the useful columns, and save the cleaned table."
      ],
      "id": "85a1ca40"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "gamesClean = (games\n",
        "    .with_columns(game_date = pl.col('game_date').str.to_date('%m/%d/%Y'))\n",
        "    .with_columns(\n",
        "        overtime = ((pl.col('game_minutes') - 240) / 25).cast(pl.Int64),\n",
        "        days_left = (pl.col('game_date').max().over('season') - pl.col('game_date')).dt.total_days(),\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .with_columns(late_season = pl.col('days_left') <= 14)\n",
        "    .select(\n",
        "        'game_id', 'game_date', 'season', 'home_team_abbr', 'away_team_abbr', 'official1', 'official2', 'official3',\n",
        "        'crew_fouls_per_game', 'crew_experience', 'crew_foul_diff', 'crew_home_win_pct',\n",
        "        'home_team_fouls', 'away_team_fouls', 'overtime', 'late_season', 'total_fouls'\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    .sort('game_date')\n",
        ")\n",
        "gamesClean.write_parquet(here('NBAFoulPredictor/Data/nba_games_clean.parquet'))\n",
        "gamesClean.shape"
      ],
      "id": "4b99b734",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The final table has **10,729 games** across **9 regular seasons** (2017–18 through 2025–26), with one row per game.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data dictionary:**\n",
        "\n",
        "| Variable | Description |\n",
        "|:--|:--|\n",
        "| `total_fouls` | **Outcome.** Personal fouls called on both teams combined |\n",
        "| `crew_fouls_per_game` | Average of the three referees' season fouls called per game |\n",
        "| `crew_experience` | Average years of NBA experience of the three referees |\n",
        "| `crew_foul_diff` | Average of (fouls on road team − fouls on home team) per game |\n",
        "| `crew_home_win_pct` | Average home-team win % in the referees' games |\n",
        "| `home_team_fouls`, `away_team_fouls` | Each team's average personal fouls per game that season |\n",
        "| `overtime` | Number of overtime periods (0–4) |\n",
        "| `late_season` | Game in the final 14 days of the regular season |\n",
        "| `season` | Season (2017–18 is the reference level) |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Note on sample size:** the assignment suggests at most 5,000 rows to reduce computation time. All models in this report fit in seconds on the full 10,729 games, so we use the full data for more precise estimates.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Exploratory Data Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "### Distribution of Total Fouls"
      ],
      "id": "53864d38"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "(ggplot(gamesClean, aes(x = 'total_fouls'))\n",
        "    + geom_histogram(binwidth = 1, fill = nbaGreen)\n",
        "    + labs(x = 'Total fouls in game', y = 'Number of games',\n",
        "           title = 'Most games have 35–44 fouls')\n",
        "    + nbaTheme\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "70b7b9e1",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
