    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Predictive Fit on Test Data"
      ],
      "id": "db771d9f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "y_pred = fit_05.predict(X_test)\n",
        "print('Test RMSE:', round(root_mean_squared_error(y_test, y_pred), 2))\n",
        "\n",
        "testPlot = pl.DataFrame({'actual': y_test.to_numpy(), 'predicted': np.asarray(y_pred)})\n",
        "\n",
        "(ggplot(testPlot, aes(x = 'predicted', y = 'actual'))\n",
        "  + geom_point(alpha = 0.15, color = nbaGreen)\n",
        "  + geom_abline(slope = 1, intercept = 0, color = 'red', linetype = '--')\n",
        "  + labs(x = 'Predicted total fouls', y = 'Actual total fouls',\n",
        "         title = 'Predictions vs. real games (test data)')\n",
        "  + nbaTheme\n",
        ")"
      ],
      "id": "0192aa1a",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Points scatter evenly around the red line (perfect prediction), with no systematic over- or under-prediction. Most test games fall within about 6 fouls of the prediction.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Decision-Theoretic Fit: Expected Quadratic Loss\n",
        "\n",
        "Our loss function is quadratic loss, so the expected loss of a forecasting approach is its average squared error on games it has not seen (test MSE). We compare the full model to two simple rules a coaching staff could use without a model."
      ],
      "id": "6d721392"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "trainSeason = gamesClean['season'].to_numpy()[X_train.index]\n",
        "testSeason = gamesClean['season'].to_numpy()[X_test.index]\n",
        "seasonMeans = pd.Series(y_train.to_numpy()).groupby(trainSeason).mean()\n",
        "\n",
        "lossTable = pl.DataFrame({\n",
        "    'forecast_rule': ['League average (all seasons)', 'Season average', 'Full model (C)'],\n",
        "    'expected_loss_MSE': [\n",
        "        mean_squared_error(y_test, np.full(len(y_test), y_train.mean())),\n",
        "        mean_squared_error(y_test, seasonMeans.loc[testSeason].to_numpy()),\n",
        "        mean_squared_error(y_test, y_pred),\n",
        "    ],\n",
        "}).with_columns(\n",
        "    pl.col('expected_loss_MSE').round(2),\n",
        "    typical_miss_fouls = pl.col('expected_loss_MSE').sqrt().round(2),\n",
        ")\n",
        "lossTable"
      ],
      "id": "52e2a96c",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "The full model has the lowest expected quadratic loss. Planning for the season average (MSE about 47) is no better than planning for the league average, while the full model lowers expected loss to about 34, a reduction of roughly 28%. In practical terms, the typical miss drops from about 6.9 to about 5.8 fouls, and large planning misses become less common. This is the measure that matches our business objective most directly.\n",
        "\n",
        "# Recommendations\n",
        "\n",
        "## Translating Crew Differences Into Free-Throw Points\n",
        "\n",
        "We predict total fouls for an average 2025–26 matchup under a low-foul crew (10th percentile of 2025–26 crews), a typical crew (median), and a high-foul crew (90th percentile), holding everything else at typical values."
      ],
      "id": "0cd01771"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "latest = gamesClean.filter(pl.col('season') == '2025-2026')\n",
        "\n",
        "crewLevels = {\n",
        "    'Low-foul crew': latest['crew_fouls_per_game'].quantile(0.10),\n",
        "    'Typical crew': latest['crew_fouls_per_game'].median(),\n",
        "    'High-foul crew': latest['crew_fouls_per_game'].quantile(0.90),\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "X_scen = pd.DataFrame(0.0, index = range(3), columns = X_train.columns)\n",
        "X_scen['const'] = 1\n",
        "X_scen['crew_fouls_per_game'] = list(crewLevels.values())\n",
        "X_scen['crew_experience'] = latest['crew_experience'].median()\n",
        "X_scen['crew_foul_diff'] = latest['crew_foul_diff'].median()\n",
        "X_scen['crew_home_win_pct'] = latest['crew_home_win_pct'].median()\n",
        "X_scen['home_team_fouls'] = latest['home_team_fouls'].median()\n",
        "X_scen['away_team_fouls'] = latest['away_team_fouls'].median()\n",
        "X_scen['season_2025_2026'] = 1\n",
        "\n",
        "scenTable = fit_05.get_prediction(X_scen).summary_frame(alpha = 0.05)\n",
        "scenTable.index = list(crewLevels.keys())\n",
        "\n",
        "## ASSUMPTION: ~1.1 free throws per foul x ~78% made = ~0.85 points per foul\n",
        "pointsPerFoul = 0.85\n",
        "extraFouls = scenTable.loc['High-foul crew', 'mean'] - scenTable.loc['Low-foul crew', 'mean']\n",
        "\n",
        "print(scenTable[['mean', 'mean_ci_lower', 'mean_ci_upper', 'obs_ci_lower', 'obs_ci_upper']].round(1))\n",
        "print(f'\\nHigh-foul vs. low-foul crew: {extraFouls:.1f} more fouls,')\n",
        "print(f'about {extraFouls * pointsPerFoul:.1f} extra free-throw points in the game.')"
      ],
      "id": "7c97fe93",
