    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "A high-foul crew adds about **4 fouls per game** compared with a low-foul crew, or about **3 to 3.5 free-throw points**. In a league where many games are decided by a few points, this is a meaningful edge to plan for. The 95% prediction intervals for any single game are wide (about ±11 fouls), so the crew shifts the *expected* game, but cannot guarantee the outcome of one game.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Case Study: Lakers vs. Warriors, October 13, 2026\n",
        "\n",
        "To test the model in a real pre-game setting, we predicted a game before it was played, using only information available at 9 AM ET on game day: the assigned crew (Mark Lindsay, Dedric Taylor, Nate Cearley) and each referee's and team's **2025–26** averages. This avoids the leakage issue described earlier, because all inputs come from the previous season."
      ],
      "id": "bd360f64"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "crewToday = [nameFix.get(r, r) for r in ['Mark Lindsay', 'Dedric Taylor', 'Nate Cearley']]\n",
        "homeTeam, awayTeam = 'LAL', 'GSW'\n",
        "\n",
        "lastRefs = refStats.filter(pl.col('season') == '2025-2026')\n",
        "statCols = ['fouls_per_game', 'experience', 'foul_diff', 'home_win_pct']\n",
        "medianRef = {k: float(v) for k, v in lastRefs.select(statCols).median().row(0, named = True).items()}\n",
        "\n",
        "crewList = []\n",
        "for r in crewToday:\n",
        "    row = lastRefs.filter(pl.col('referee') == r)\n",
        "    if row.height == 0:\n",
        "        print(f'{r} not found in 2025-2026 stats, using a typical referee instead.')\n",
        "        crewList.append(medianRef)\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        crewList.append({k: float(v) for k, v in row.select(statCols).row(0, named = True).items()})\n",
        "crewNow = pl.DataFrame(crewList)\n",
        "\n",
        "def teamFouls(abbr):\n",
        "    return latest.filter(pl.col('home_team_abbr') == abbr)['home_team_fouls'][0]\n",
        "\n",
        "rowNames = ['Actual crew (Oct 13)', 'Low-foul crew', 'Typical crew', 'High-foul crew']\n",
        "X_new = pd.DataFrame(0.0, index = range(4), columns = X_train.columns)\n",
        "X_new['const'] = 1\n",
        "X_new['crew_fouls_per_game'] = [crewNow['fouls_per_game'].mean()] + list(crewLevels.values())\n",
        "X_new['crew_experience'] = [crewNow['experience'].mean()] + [latest['crew_experience'].median()] * 3\n",
        "X_new['crew_foul_diff'] = [crewNow['foul_diff'].mean()] + [latest['crew_foul_diff'].median()] * 3\n",
        "X_new['crew_home_win_pct'] = [crewNow['home_win_pct'].mean()] + [latest['crew_home_win_pct'].median()] * 3\n",
        "X_new['home_team_fouls'] = teamFouls(homeTeam)\n",
        "X_new['away_team_fouls'] = teamFouls(awayTeam)\n",
        "X_new['season_2025_2026'] = 1   ## closest season in the data\n",
        "\n",
        "predTable = fit_05.get_prediction(X_new).summary_frame(alpha = 0.05)\n",
        "predTable['crew'] = rowNames\n",
        "\n",
        "actualFouls = 50   ## from the official box score (both teams' personal fouls)\n",
        "\n",
        "p = predTable.iloc[0]\n",
        "print(f\"Predicted: {p['mean']:.0f} fouls (95% prediction interval {p['obs_ci_lower']:.0f} to {p['obs_ci_upper']:.0f})\")\n",
        "print(f'Actual: {actualFouls} fouls | Inside interval: {p.obs_ci_lower <= actualFouls <= p.obs_ci_upper}')"
      ],
      "id": "0ed96628",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
